'Correct. The argument\'s entire force comes from the combination of prejudgment and a deciding vote. This principle makes exactly that combination the trigger for reconsideration — matching the argument\'s scope and strength precisely.',
'This would require rehearings whenever anyone voices any opinion, which goes far beyond the argument\'s focus on a prejudging deciding voter. A principle that justifies much more than the argument claims is the too-strong trap.',
'Jury impartiality in criminal trials is a different domain from administrative rehearings. The argument never invokes criminal procedure, so this principle changes the subject: the scope-shift trap.',
'Read carefully: this says rehearings are available only for decisions by fully impartial boards — which would exclude this very case. It reverses the needed logic and is the reverses-conditional trap.',
